<%@ page contentType="text/html;charset=UTF-8" pageEncoding="UTF-8" %><%@ include file="header.jspf" %>
<% String infoView = (String)request.getAttribute("view"); String contactEmail = (String)request.getAttribute("supportEmail"); %>
<main id="main" class="container info-page">
<nav class="info-nav" aria-label="About Dibsly"><a href="<%=base%>/about" <%=infoView.equals("about")?"aria-current=\"page\"":""%>>About</a><a href="<%=base%>/contact" <%=infoView.equals("contact")?"aria-current=\"page\"":""%>>Contact</a><a href="<%=base%>/privacy" <%=infoView.equals("privacy")?"aria-current=\"page\"":""%>>Privacy Policy</a></nav>
<% if(infoView.equals("about")){ %>
<header class="info-heading"><h1>About Dibsly.<br>Good work starts with <em>a good fit.</em></h1><p class="lede">A place for people with ideas to meet people who know how to bring them to life.</p></header>
<div class="info-layout"><aside class="info-aside"><h2>Your gig.<br>Their pitch.<br>Your pick.</h2><p>You set the outcome. Freelancers bring the approach. You choose the collaboration.</p><a class="underlink" href="<%=base%>/explore">Explore projects <%=arrow()%></a></aside><article class="info-copy">
<section><h2>A brief before a search.</h2><p>Finding a collaborator starts with explaining what you want to make. On Dibsly, clients publish a project brief, set a budget, and share when they want to get started. Freelancers respond with a plan tailored to that project.</p></section>
<section><h2>Compare the whole proposal.</h2><p>A useful pitch is more than a price. Compare the approach, deliverables, delivery time, and included support side by side. Pitches are private to the freelancer who wrote them, the client who owns the project, and administrators.</p><p>When the client accepts a pitch, Dibsly records the agreement and keeps the project in both participants’ workspaces.</p></section>
<section><h2>Clear expectations, from the start.</h2><p>Clients can close an open project. Freelancers can withdraw a pending pitch. Accepted work can be marked complete by the client. Dibsly records quotes and agreements; this release does not collect payments, hold escrow, or offer payment protection.</p></section>
<section><h2>Built to learn, made to work.</h2><p>Dibsly grew from a Java reverse-marketplace project. This version is a working demonstration of freelance collaboration and access controls. When the demo banner is visible, the seeded people and projects are fictional examples.</p><p>Accounts have permissions suited to their role. Clients manage their own projects, freelancers manage their own pitches, and administrators can restrict or restore account access.</p></section>
<div class="info-next"><h2>Have a question or an idea?</h2><a class="button" href="<%=base%>/contact">Get in touch <%=arrow()%></a></div>
</article></div>
<% } else if(infoView.equals("contact")){ %>
<header class="info-heading"><h1>Contact Dibsly.<br>Let’s <em>talk.</em></h1><p class="lede">A question about a project, something that isn’t working, or an idea for what comes next? We’d like to hear it.</p></header>
<div class="info-layout"><aside class="info-aside contact-details"><h2>Write to us.</h2><a class="contact-address" href="mailto:<%=e(contactEmail)%>"><%=e(contactEmail)%></a><p>This is our current inbox for support, feedback, and privacy requests.</p><a class="button" href="mailto:<%=e(contactEmail)%>?subject=Dibsly%20support">Email Dibsly <%=arrow()%></a><p class="hint">Opens your email app. You can also copy the address into your preferred email service.</p></aside><article class="info-copy">
<section><h2>Help us help you.</h2><p>For a support request, include your Dibsly username, the project title or page address, and a short description of what happened. If you saw an error, include its wording and the steps that led to it.</p><p>Please don’t send passwords, session tokens, payment details, or confidential project files.</p></section>
<section><h2>Your data, your questions.</h2><p>Use the same inbox to ask about your information or request access, correction, or deletion. Tell us which account the request concerns; we may need to verify your identity before acting on it.</p><a class="underlink" href="<%=base%>/privacy">Read our Privacy Policy <%=arrow()%></a></section>
<section><h2>A few answers, right here.</h2><details open><summary>Does Dibsly handle payments?</summary><p>This release records quotes and agreements but does not process payments or provide escrow. Arrange payment separately with your collaborator.</p></details><details><summary>Who can see a freelancer’s pitch?</summary><p>The freelancer who submitted it, the project’s client, and administrators. Competing freelancers cannot view it.</p></details><details><summary>Can I recover a forgotten password?</summary><p>Self-service password recovery is not available in this release. Email support for help with your account; don’t send your password.</p></details><a class="underlink" href="<%=base%>/how-it-works">More about how Dibsly works <%=arrow()%></a></section>
</article></div>
<% } else { %>
<header class="info-heading"><h1>Privacy Policy.<br>Your information, <em>explained.</em></h1><p class="lede">What this version of Dibsly stores, why it uses it, and who can see it.</p><p class="quiet">Last updated: 27 October 2026</p></header>
<div class="info-layout"><aside class="info-aside"><h2>On this page</h2><nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Privacy sections"><a href="#scope">Who this covers</a><a href="#information">Information we use</a><a href="#visibility">Who can see it</a><a href="#storage">Cookies & browser storage</a><a href="#retention">Keeping your information</a><a href="#choices">Your choices & requests</a><a href="#changes">Changes to this notice</a></nav><p>Questions? <a href="<%=base%>/contact">Contact Dibsly</a>.</p></aside><article class="info-copy">
<section id="scope"><h2>Who this covers</h2><p>This notice describes the current Dibsly marketplace application, including its local demonstration. The person or organisation running your Dibsly instance manages its stored information. For this instance, contact the operator at <a href="mailto:<%=e(contactEmail)%>"><%=e(contactEmail)%></a>.</p><p>Demo accounts and seeded projects are fictional. Information you enter yourself is still stored, so use sample details when trying the demonstration.</p></section>
<section id="information"><h2>Information we use</h2><ul><li><strong>Account details:</strong> your display name, username, chosen role, account status, and creation date. Passwords are stored as salted hashes, rather than readable passwords.</li><li><strong>Marketplace activity:</strong> project briefs, categories, budgets, start preferences, pitches, quotes, delivery and support terms, agreement dates, and project status.</li><li><strong>Access and security records:</strong> permission changes and audit events describing protected actions. The server uses an IP address and username to limit repeated failed login attempts.</li><li><strong>Support correspondence:</strong> if you email us, your email provider and the support inbox handle your address, message, and any attachments.</li></ul><p>We use this information to sign you in, show relevant work, share proposals with the intended participants, record agreements, respond to requests, and enforce access controls. Registration does not currently ask for an email address. The application does not collect card details or process payments.</p></section>
<section id="visibility"><h2>Who can see it</h2><p>Open project briefs, budgets, and the client’s displayed name are visible to visitors. Keep private contact information and confidential material out of public briefs.</p><p>A pitch is visible to its author, the client who owns the project, and administrators. Closed project details are restricted to the owner, administrators, and freelancers with a pitch on that project. Administrators can inspect account and audit information to operate the service.</p><p>The application does not include advertising trackers, third-party analytics, or data-sale integrations. Its fonts and assets are served locally. If deployed, hosting, database, backup, and email providers may process information for the operator. Their identities, locations, and any international transfers depend on that deployment and have not been specified for this local demonstration.</p></section>
<section id="storage"><h2>Cookies & browser storage</h2><p>Dibsly uses an essential session cookie to maintain your browser session and protect forms. Server sessions expire after 30 minutes of inactivity; signing out invalidates the current session. Blocking this cookie prevents account features from working.</p><p>Unpublished project drafts are saved in your browser’s tab storage to help you recover work after a reload. Drafts are removed after successful publication, and tab storage normally clears when the tab closes. Your browser’s session-restore features may retain a tab. Clear site data when using a shared device. Drafts are sent to the server when you submit the form.</p><p>This release does not set advertising or analytics cookies.</p></section>
<section id="retention"><h2>Keeping your information</h2><p>Accounts, projects, pitches, agreements, and audit records persist in the application database until the operator removes them. This release has no automatic deletion schedule or self-service account deletion. A cancelled project or withdrawn pitch remains a stored record.</p><p>Login-throttling records are held in server memory. Their blocking window is 15 minutes; records clear on successful login, on an expired entry being checked, or when the server restarts. Server logs and backups, if enabled by the operator, have separate retention settings.</p><p>Access checks, password hashing, and restricted session cookies help protect information. Public hosting also requires HTTPS and appropriate database and backup controls. No system can guarantee absolute security.</p></section>
<section id="choices"><h2>Your choices & requests</h2><p>You can browse public projects without an account and choose what to include in your briefs and pitches. To request access, correction, or deletion of stored information, email <a href="mailto:<%=e(contactEmail)%>?subject=Dibsly%20privacy%20request"><%=e(contactEmail)%></a>. Include your username and the nature of your request, but never your password. The operator may need to verify your identity and consider records involving other participants.</p><p>Privacy rights and any applicable complaint route depend on your location and the operator’s legal obligations. This demo notice does not claim compliance with a particular jurisdiction. Before a public launch, the operator must identify its legal entity, applicable processing grounds, service providers, retention rules, and local rights procedures.</p></section>
<section id="changes"><h2>Changes to this notice</h2><p>When the application’s data practices change, this page should be updated with a new revision date. Review it before sharing new information, and <a href="<%=base%>/contact">contact us</a> if anything is unclear.</p></section>
</article></div>
<% } %>
</main><%@ include file="footer.jspf" %>
